SYNTHESIS
  Naive coordinatewise residual dominance is false: spread shapes can cover
  small specified residual sets better than the consecutive block.
  The full-cover scalar and the HYP-2694 split-context beam still point to
  consecutive/coherent blocks as the dangerous shapes.
  New proof target: characterize the residual-profile cone generated by
  decorrelated LRC contexts and prove consecutive maximizes the weighted
  capacity functional on that cone.  Then combine with THM-557's split
  gaps and the joint carrier error budget.
  No LRC14 proof is claimed.
